--- Technical ---
### Changed

- Integrate the complete M9 Frontend Redesign into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes so the release can be tagged from one coherent point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown, anchoring each badge after its cited passage title and retaining unanchored citations in the numbered sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Represent `SuggestedNextSteps` as `IReadOnlyList<SuggestedStep>` and make its first actionable item the ticket-header primary control. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable `CommandPalette` to `MainLayout`, opened with Ctrl/Cmd+K, with navigation entries from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Add optimistic status updates to board and detail views, reconciling successful board moves with server state and restoring the prior state when a transition is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that apply changes without leaving the ticket. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges by matching each `AssistantCitation` title to the answer text, retaining unmatched citations in the numbered sources list. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster, including an explicit empty-roster state, to each chat system prompt via `GetAgentsHandler`, and direct the assistant to use only listed names for assignments. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to invoke `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` once after retrieval and before the first streamed token. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Replace scattered frontend style literals with shared design tokens for palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors, exposed as root custom properties and reused by `AppTheme`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Fix board card title clamping by wrapping the title link so `-webkit-line-clamp` is not blockified by the grid layout. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant panel styling by targeting `.assistant-chat` through `::deep`, restoring its padding and flex layout so the send button stays inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Fix the ticket queue header overlap by giving the Category column a 140px width and applying the uppercase label styling used by neighboring headers. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add chat system-prompt rules requiring a successful tool result before claiming a change and avoiding repeated confirmation of a requested change unless a genuine user decision is needed. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket-summary timestamps to the request's `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Fix `search_knowledge_base` so failed searches return `IsError: true`, while unavailable searches remain distinct non-error results. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Replace lexical-only grounding evaluation with sentence-level semantic similarity to retrieved passages, retaining `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as a fallback when embeddings are unavailable or fail. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
