    ! #237: "When a ticket has an actionable suggestion, its first suggested step appears as a primary button or owner picker" - PR #237 says actionable steps are ordered first, but the primary control depends on the action: a status change gets a button and assignment gets an agent picker. The wording implies any actionable suggestion produces either control without that qualification.
    ! #218: "the product now tells the assistant and autonomous worker to check a draft against them before streaming an answer" - PR #218 says the check is enforced through `tool_choice`, not merely requested. Describing the change as telling them to check understates the mechanism that was added.

